#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_drop_from

#% text
# `key_drop_from(a, k)` removes the key `k` (or the keys of a list) from the association held by the symbol `a`, stores the result back in `a` and gives it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
a = assoc(x -> 1, y -> 2, z -> 3)

#% cell
key_drop_from(a, x)
#% output
#= assoc(y -> 2, z -> 3)

#% cell
key_drop_from(a, [y, w])
#% output
#= assoc(z -> 3)

#% cell
a
#% output
#= assoc(z -> 3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `associate_to`, `key_drop`
